SYMATTR InstName R1
SYMATTR Value {RFX}
SYMBOL cap 144 320 R0
SYMATTR InstName C1
SYMATTR Value {CFX}
SYMBOL res 368 320 R0
SYMATTR InstName R1ref
SYMATTR Value {RFX}
SYMBOL cap 592 320 R0
SYMATTR InstName C1ref
SYMATTR Value {CFX}
SYMBOL cap 816 320 R0
SYMATTR InstName CL
SYMATTR Value {CLOAD}
SYMBOL res 1040 320 R0
SYMATTR InstName RL
SYMATTR Value {RLOAD}
SYMBOL SpecialFunctions\sample 176 576 R0
SYMATTR InstName A1
SYMBOL SpecialFunctions\sample 624 576 R0
SYMATTR InstName A2
TEXT 32 864 Left 2 !.param AMP=2 RF=330 CF=10n CLOAD=1.5p RLOAD=8Meg
TEXT 32 896 Left 2 !;.param RF=4.7k CF=1n
TEXT 32 928 Left 2 !.param RFX=mc(RF,0.01) CFX=mc(CF,0.05)
TEXT 32 960 Left 2 !.param FS=160k NCH=8 TGND=200n TADC=488n
TEXT 32 992 Left 2 !.param TFRAME={1/FS} TSIG={TFRAME/NCH-TGND} T0={TFRAME-TSIG} TM0={T0+TADC+1u}
TEXT 32 1024 Left 2 !.tran 0 3.3333m 0
TEXT 32 1056 Left 2 !.meas TRAN err_max MAX V(errh) FROM {TM0} TO 3.3333m
TEXT 32 1088 Left 2 !.meas TRAN err_min MIN V(errh) FROM {TM0} TO 3.3333m
TEXT 32 1120 Left 2 !.meas TRAN err_rms RMS V(errh) FROM {TM0} TO 3.3333m
TEXT 32 1152 Left 2 !.meas TRAN err_pk_ppm PARAM max(abs(err_max),abs(err_min))/AMP*1e6
TEXT 32 1184 Left 2 !.meas TRAN ref_rms RMS V(refh) FROM {TM0} TO 3.3333m
TEXT 32 1216 Left 2 !.meas TRAN sxy INTEG V(errh)*V(refh) FROM {TM0} TO 3.3333m
TEXT 32 1248 Left 2 !.meas TRAN sxx INTEG V(refh)*V(refh) FROM {TM0} TO 3.3333m
TEXT 32 1280 Left 2 !.meas TRAN gain_ppm PARAM sxy/sxx*1e6
TEXT 32 1312 Left 2 !.meas TRAN resid_rms PARAM sqrt(max(err_rms*err_rms-(sxy/sxx*ref_rms)*(sxy/sxx*ref_rms),0))
TEXT 32 1344 Left 2 !.meas TRAN filt_dip MIN V(filt)-V(ref) FROM 0 TO 3.3333m
TEXT 32 1392 Left 2 ;SPICA sample: MUX507_2TO1 (+-5 V) reading an RC-filtered 3 kHz sine in a scan. S0 = signal, S1 = GND (discharge).
TEXT 32 1424 Left 2 ;FS = sample rate per channel; frame 1/FS = NCH x (TGND + TSIG). Per channel: GND for TGND (200 ns), then the input for TSIG
TEXT 32 1456 Left 2 ;(781.25 - 200 = 581.25 ns), once every 6.25 us. Change TGND and TSIG follows.
TEXT 32 1488 Left 2 ;the rest of the frame D sits on GND. The other channels are each preceded by a GND slot, so D is at 0 V whenever this channel connects.
TEXT 32 1520 Left 2 ;The ADC samples TADC after the channel-selection edge (488 ns); A1 holds V(da)-V(ref), A2 holds V(ref).
TEXT 32 1552 Left 2 ;At +-5 V the switch connects ~140 ns after the edge and turns off ~90 ns after the slot ends: keep TADC inside that window.
TEXT 32 1584 Left 2 ;err_* = sampled error vs the same filter without the mux (V). gain_ppm = least-squares gain error of the samples (= RMS-reading error);
TEXT 32 1616 Left 2 ;resid_rms = what is left, mostly an ~8 ns timing shift of the sampled waveform (does not change an RMS reading).
TEXT 32 1648 Left 2 ;filt_dip = deepest dip on the filter node. CLOAD/RLOAD = op-amp input on D. Swap the RF/CF lines for 4.7k/1n.
TEXT 32 1680 Left 2 ;U1 carries the uniform Monte Carlo defaults; set RONK=1 CKS=1 CKD=1 QK=0 on U1 (SpiceLine) for a nominal part.
